cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below, and record the exact commit you used.
title: 'growth-rates-lean: Fekete-type growth rates, uniform envelopes and finite-time errors in Lean 4'
type: software
authors:
- family-names: Chen
  given-names: Le
  affiliation: Auburn University
license: Apache-2.0
# version, date-released and the Zenodo DOI are set at the first release.
repository-code: https://github.com/chenle02/growth-rates-lean
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 library on growth rates of real functions of a real time variable. It proves Fekete's lemma in
  continuous time: if b is nonnegative, subadditive on [0, infinity) and bounded above on bounded intervals,
  then b(t)/t converges to the infimum of b(h)/h over h > 0. It transfers this rate to functions within a
  logarithmic error of b, proves a Fekete lemma with a logarithmic defect a(x) + a(y) - M log(x + y) - B <=
  a(x + y) whose limit is an explicit supremum of corrected slopes, with delayed and multiplicative forms,
  derives uniform and joint limits over an order parameter from fixed-order limits and one uniform lower
  error, and turns cut, confinement and composition inequalities into an explicit finite-time error
  |log f(T) - T lambda| <= n (1 + log(2 + T lambda / n)). All such inequalities are hypotheses.
keywords:
- Lean 4
- Mathlib
- formalization
- Fekete's lemma
- subadditive functions
- growth rate
- near-subadditive
- uniform limits
- finite-time error
references:
- type: conference-paper
  title: The Lean Mathematical Library
  authors:
  - name: The mathlib Community
  collection-title: 'Proceedings of the 9th ACM SIGPLAN International Conference on Certified Programs and Proofs (CPP 2020)'
  year: 2020
  doi: 10.1145/3372885.3373824
  repository-code: https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4
